WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.241
Today I am going to tell you about one of
my favourite results, Bell's theorem, that

00:00:05.241 --> 00:00:08.000
answers the EPR paradox.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.559
But instead of proving the thing here, I've
decided to push that to the next video, and

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:17.020
instead just tell you the result and explain
what it actually means.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:21.019
That's because this is the most misunderstood
theorem of science that I know of.

00:00:21.019 --> 00:00:26.779
I have heard it claimed by so many sources,
from popular books, to lecturers, to serious

00:00:26.779 --> 00:00:32.390
research papers that Bell's theorem proves
quantum mechanics is right Let's see if that's

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:34.040
true

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:38.110
We've already seen that quantum mechanics
has a few disturbing aspects.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:42.670
I'd argue that a lot that comes done to one
statement in quantum mechanics, the superposition

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:46.960
principle; that is that if we have a particle
that could be in several possible states at

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:53.150
a certain time and we can't tell which one
its in, it's in all those states at once.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:57.820
That means that while we have our backs turned,
things act way differently to how they act

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.730
when we're looking.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.850
But do we have to really believe that?

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:07.080
I mean, we can never, by definition actually
catch the objects in the act.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.740
The EPR paradox tried to prove that superposition
is wrong.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.570
I won't go through the EPR argument in detail
again because you can just watch that video

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:18.380
once more if you need a refresher

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:23.069
Remember for the EPR video, we had our two
entangled objects and we knew one was red

00:01:23.069 --> 00:01:26.649
and other white, but we didn't know which
was which.

00:01:26.649 --> 00:01:31.630
Quantum Mechanics insists that all possible
things happen so each particle is both red

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:33.159
and white.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:38.390
But if we open one box and the object is white,
then when we open the other we must have the

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:39.740
red one.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:44.990
The only way is if, somehow or another, the
particles can talk to each other.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:49.510
We'll call any theory where entangled particles
are able to communicate while they're separated

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:52.299
like this, a theory with "talking particles"

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:55.340
But the EPR argument then showed that

00:01:55.340 --> 00:02:01.259
If a theory has talking particles, then those
messages go faster than light.

00:02:01.259 --> 00:02:02.909
So what does this mean?

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:06.950
If Einstein and the majority of physicists
at the time where right and nothing can ever

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:13.700
faster then light, then EPR tells us that
all theories with talking particles are wrong.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.690
That includes quantum mechanics.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:21.130
If nothing truly can go faster than light,
how can we explain the fact that entangled

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:24.580
particles always have opposite colours to
each other?

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:29.310
They can't talk talk to each other while they're
seperated as EPR shows, so they must decide

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:32.500
which colours to be while they're still together.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:36.380
That means that instead of acting all crazy
and going into superpositions while they're

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:41.700
behind our backs, they instead act pretty
normal with just one colour.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:46.200
SO you see, if nothing can go faster than
the speed of light, not only is Quantum mechanics

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:50.600
done for, we can go back to believing the
world isn't doing such crazy things while

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:51.750
we're not looking.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:58.290
I.e if particle's can't talk faster than light,
then superposition is wrong.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.820
What about the other possibility?

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:04.740
What if entangled particles do talk faster
than light to each other?

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:09.430
This is where lots of people get it wrong
so I urge you to be careful.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:15.650
if entangled particles do talk faster than
light that doesn't necessarily imply superposition

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.280
is right.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.740
That would be like saying
If an animal is a raven it is black

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:24.590
Means that
If an animal isn't a raven then its not black.

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:26.850
That's clearly not true.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:32.190
If an animal isn't a raven, all you can say
is that its not raven, you can't infer anything

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.930
about its colour.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:39.680
In the same way, if particles talk faster
than light, all you can say is, they do talk

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.600
faster than light.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:45.390
SO finally we get to the point.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.360
What is Bell's theorem.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:51.660
Bell came up with an experiment that would
give different results in a world where particles

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:55.690
can talk faster than light and one where they
can't.

00:03:55.690 --> 00:04:00.390
This got people really excited because there
was a chance to disprove quantum mechanics.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:06.110
15 years later, people finally came up with
the technology to do the experiment.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.800
There result?

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:10.890
Particles do actually do talk faster than
light.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:12.770
Quantum mechanics survived.

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:18.380
But like I said before, this doesn't prove
Quantum mechanics is right, only that it isn't

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:20.459
wrong in this way.

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:23.250
This brings up a lot questions.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:25.750
Firstly, what about relativity?

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:31.290
Remember I told you that the biggest assumption
in relativity is that nothing goes faster

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:35.810
than light, but apparently that's not true!

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:40.650
I don't know enough relativity to teach it
to you, but in relativity, if it's possible

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:46.710
for Alice to send Bob a message faster than
light, all kinds of crazy stuff can happen.

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:52.290
For example, to some people it will look like
Bob gets Alice's message before she sends

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:53.410
it.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:58.410
It's even possible for him to reply before
she sends it- but then -what if she decided

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:01.150
not to send her original message afterall?

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:04.900
That is an aweful logical mess.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:08.150
So what's the solution?

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:10.720
Physicists say that they have come up with
it.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:15.650
They claim that it's impossible to manipulate
our entangled talking particles to send the

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:17.600
messages we want.

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:20.380
This is called the No Communication theorem.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:26.000
I don't know if we should just trust though,
so we'll have a closer look at it later.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:32.020
Another question is that, sure, this experiment
doesn't prove that superposition is true,

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:36.180
but is it really possible to explain all the
weird experiments we've been talking about

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:37.650
with out it?

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:40.050
Turns out it might be.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:45.300
There is at least one very promising alternative
to quantum mechanics that does have talking

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:50.150
particles so it's not ruled out, but doesn't
have superposition.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:56.650
It's called Bohmian Mechanics, and I might
make a video about it cos it's pretty amazing.

00:05:56.650 --> 00:06:01.540
So that's the end of this video but if you
want to see how Bell's theorem proves that

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:08.210
particles can talk faster than light, then
I will be putting up videos about that.

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:12.790
They'll be one to explain something called
Spin and then the actual proof.

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:16.590
If you don't know too much about spin, you
should watch that one first.

